  description: Dubnium is a chemical element with symbol Db and atomic number 105.
    It is named after the town of Dubna in Russia (north of Moscow), where it was
    first produced. It is a synthetic element (an element that can be created in
    a laboratory but is not found in nature) and radioactive; the most stable known
    isotope, dubnium-268, has a half-life of approximately 28 hours.
